313	FACTS.md:86
314	- **The `XXX` expected-failure mechanism in `compiler_tests/` and `library_tests/` can express a compile-stage failure only, and a run-time defect needs two `.test` files** (2026-09-20, rung B). `shouldFail` comes from the `.test` file name (`FileTests.java:932`) and the same flag reaches every stage the file drives (`:1052-1059`, `:1063-1069`), so an `XXX` file that carries `link` or `compile` demands that the compile fail (`:384-404`, message at `:402`); and a `TestTest` fails on an unsatisfied `run_out_*` verdict whatever `shouldFail` says (`:534-539`, `:583-585`), with `pass`/`PASS` demanded by default when no check is set (`:276-282`). Of the 224 `XXX*.test` files that were in `compiler_tests/` before this batch, 223 drive `compile`, one drives `link`, none drives `run`. A compiles-but-crashes defect is therefore gated as two `.test` files over one component — a plain-named one driving `link`, an `XXX`-named one driving `run` with a marker the failing run does print — which is what rung B did and showed going red on a deliberate fix (`compile-ladder/rung-tryatomic/raw/junit-xxx-expected.txt`, `raw/junit-xxx-goes-red.txt`), and what the gather reused for rung W's row 348.
315	
316	FACTS.md:83
317	- **The gate's thread count is pinned in the build file, not in the calling shell** (2026-09-19, `build.xml:947` in the `fastTrack` macro, beside `systemShard`'s own at `:1188`): `<env key="FORTRESS_THREADS" value="1"/>`. Before it, `fastTrack` set only `FORTRESS_CACHES`; the forked JUnit JVM and the per-test subprocess inherited the caller's environment (`FileTests.java:482-486`), `getNumThreads` otherwise takes `floor(nproc/2)` (`FortressExecutable.java:37-44`), and the `1` came from `explorations/experiment/env.sh:6` — so `ant testFast` from a shell that had not sourced `env.sh`, which is what CI and Pavol's machine would do, ran `compiler_tests` at a different count and proved something else. Verified directly: with `FORTRESS_THREADS=4` exported in the calling shell, `ant -v testFast` logs `Setting environment variable: FORTRESS_THREADS=1` for each of the four `fastTrack` forks. `env.sh`'s line is now a convenience rather than the definition.
